# .gitignore for a Quartus + ModelSim + Verilator project.
#
# The rule: commit SOURCE, ignore anything a tool can regenerate.
#
# A Quartus project generates hundreds of megabytes of databases and reports,
# and they change on every compile -- committing them makes the repository huge,
# makes every `git diff` unreadable, and guarantees annoying merge conflicts.
#
# COMMIT these (they are your project, and they are all text):
#   *.qpf *.qsf *.sdc      the project itself
#   rtl/ tb/ scripts/      your code
#   *.md                   your notes

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Quartus generated directories
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
db/
incremental_db/
greybox_tmp/
.qsys_edit/
simulation/
timing/

# Compile output: reports, netlists, and the bitstream itself. All rebuildable
# from source in a couple of minutes.
output_files/

# A pin-model debug dump the fitter writes into the project root:
c5_pin_model_dump.txt

# Quartus workspace/session state -- per-user, not per-project.
# (*.sof is ignored too: the ONE exception is your final .sof for submission,
# which you `git add -f` at the very end -- see docs/GIT_WITH_QUARTUS.md.)
*.qws
*.bak
*.rpt.bak
*.done
*.smsg
*.pin
*.sof
*.pof
*.jdi
*.qar
*.qdf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ModelSim
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
sim_modelsim/
work/
transcript
vsim.wlf
modelsim.ini
*.mti
*.wlf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Verilator
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
sim_verilator/
obj_dir/

# Waveforms: large and regenerated by scripts/simulate.py.
*.vcd
*.fst

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python caches the compiled form of scripts/common.py here the first time
# another script imports it. It is regenerated automatically:
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and operating systems
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.vscode/settings.json
